OL,3,GNEWSA'Motorway closures mean we can't
OL,4,Asleep at night'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA couple have said they cannot sleep
OL,7,Fdue to traffic being diverted past
OL,8,Ftheir home at night during long-running
OL,9,Fmotorway improvements.
OL,11,FThe M67 has been closed in both
OL,12,Fdirections on weeknights between 20:00
OL,13,Fand 06:00 since July and lorries and
OL,14,Fcars will continue to be diverted onto
OL,15,FMottram Road, in Godley, Tameside,
OL,16,Funtil December.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,409,400,260,160,0,100
PN,40802
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F408A1792506411
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kj 5j js17kjc15 js57kj#4
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,-. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,! ,,
OL,3,GNEWSA'Motorway closures mean we can't
OL,4,Asleep at night'
OL,5,
OL,6,FFrancoise Sullivan, who has lived on
OL,7,Fthe road since 1987, said: "It's a
OL,8,Fnightmare - we just can't sleep from
OL,9,Fthe noise and the vibrations. We've
OL,10,Fbeen given some medication but it
OL,11,Fdoesn't really help because the house
OL,12,Fshakes, the bed shakes and we worry
OL,13,Fwhat it's doing to our house."
OL,15,FNational Highways said it "understands"
OL,16,Fthe impact roadworks can have on local
OL,17,Fpeople.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
